==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Macho Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Mohawk Cat''' at level 20+10 using [[Normal Cat Capsule|Cat Tickets]].

==Strategy/Usage==
A basic unit with low health and attack power, and no special abilities; you will need more than this cat alone in later stages. Fortunately, it is cheap and has a short recharge time so it can be spammed. Alongside [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]] and others of its likeness, Cat can be used to slow down or even immobilize enemies completely by acting as a meatshield. Using this compensation with hard-hitters behind the numbers creates a wall that approaches the enemy base slowly, but surely. On his own, however, it gets overshadowed by Tank Cat as the latter is designed to better resist attacks and hold ground. There are still situations where Cat is the better choice, being against enemies and situations where Tank's extra health does not matter, due to how strong the enemy attacks are.

Another good aspect of this unit is that it appears in many [[Cat Combo]]s, most notably [[Cat Army (Combo)|Cat Army]], suited for the very beginning of the game, and [[Mo' Hawks (Combo)|Mo' Hawks]] for mid-game. Hence, you should not underestimate its potential.

==='''True Form'''===
Mohawk Cat gains double its original health and attack power in True Form, which allows it to solo stages on most beginner stages and chapters. However, the boost in stats is not enough to give Mohawk Cat any other role besides cannon fodder. This form, however, still allows it to sometimes survive an attack from a weak peon that his previous forms would not handle as well; but in [[Uncanny Legends]] and late-game [[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]], this makes little or no difference. Therefore, it is important to note that without an overabundance of "+" levels, Mohawk Cat will not be any more useful than any other meatshield of the same cost.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield}}

